lobby-tutorial-basics-title = WHAT THIS IS
lobby-tutorial-basics-intro = Grosse Alliance is a roleplay server for Space Station 14 set in the Half-Life 2 universe. The city here is called City 14, and it is laid out like City 17 from the original game. It is not a space station full of nuclear operatives and cultists.
lobby-tutorial-basics-setting = The setting sets it apart at once. Instead of Nanotrasen and space there is the totalitarian Combine regime on Earth. Instead of a station there is a city split into sectors, with a train station, plazas and residential blocks.
lobby-tutorial-basics-departments = The usual departments such as cargo, science and medbay are gone. Civil Protection keeps order, the Civil Workers Union hands out jobs, and everyone else lives as an ordinary citizen.
lobby-tutorial-basics-death = This is hard roleplay with permanent death. A dead character does not come back to the same role in this round, and the only exceptions are special mechanics such as the refugee lottery.
lobby-tutorial-basics-mood = The atmosphere is built on control, fear, shortages and propaganda. It is not a cheerful space sandbox but a grim occupied world.
lobby-tutorial-basics-tone = Hence the first rule: play a person who lives in this city. Everything the character does, he does because there is no other way.
lobby-tutorial-basics-box = [bold]Remember.[/bold] This is not space. There are no station laws here, but there are patrols, ration tickets and a CID card.

lobby-tutorial-controls-title = CONTROLS
lobby-tutorial-controls-intro = Controls are almost entirely standard for SS14, and they can be rebound with F10 in the Controls tab. Below is what you will need in the first minutes.
lobby-tutorial-act-move = Walking
lobby-tutorial-act-walk = Slow walk, hold the key
lobby-tutorial-act-use = Interact with an object
lobby-tutorial-act-click = Use the object under the cursor
lobby-tutorial-act-item = Use the item in your hand
lobby-tutorial-act-alt = Alternative item action
lobby-tutorial-act-examine = Examine an item
lobby-tutorial-act-chat = Open chat
lobby-tutorial-act-radio = Radio and local channel
lobby-tutorial-act-drop = Drop an item
lobby-tutorial-act-throw = Throw towards the cursor
lobby-tutorial-act-settings = Settings menu
lobby-tutorial-controls-binds = Binds can be changed to taste, but the defaults are worth learning: other players rely on them when they say press E. Radio only works with a headset, and a loud conversation is heard by everyone standing nearby.
lobby-tutorial-controls-pace = Walking on WASD and looking around with the mouse come from other games, but shift-walking is worth learning at once. Running is heard through a wall, and a patrol comes to a noise faster than to a violation.
lobby-tutorial-controls-box = [bold]Tip.[/bold] Check your binds before the first patrol. During a raid it is too late to open the settings.

lobby-tutorial-rules-title = HL2RP RULES
lobby-tutorial-rules-intro = This is the base that gets you punished on HL2 servers, up to a permanent ban. The server is advertised as hard roleplay, so the rules are stricter than on a normal station.
lobby-tutorial-rules-death = Death is final. After dying the character is gone for the round, you cannot return to the same role, and knowledge gained after death does not come back into play.
lobby-tutorial-rules-nonrp = NonRP is failing to play the role, not reacting to what happens around you or breaking the logic of the world. The examples are simple: a citizen attacks a Civil Protection patrol with bare fists, or a CP officer befriends citizens and ignores violations.
lobby-tutorial-rules-fear = FearRP is playing fear for your life. Under a gun the character obeys, trembles, begs for mercy or looks for a safe way out. Drawing a weapon in response, running in a straight line or ignoring the threat is forbidden.
lobby-tutorial-rules-pg = PowerGaming is exceeding the character's limits. Without armour and a weapon he will not knock out three CP soldiers, and a citizen does not know where the secret Resistance base is.
lobby-tutorial-rules-nlr = NLR, the new life rule. After death the character does not remember the killer, does not take revenge on him and does not act on knowledge from the previous life.
lobby-tutorial-rules-meta = MetaGaming is using information from outside the game. Discord, a stream and a voice call in another program give the character nothing.
lobby-tutorial-rules-hunt = Role hunting is joining the server only for one specific role, for example rejoining to get CP. Leaving the round to take another role is not allowed either.
lobby-tutorial-rules-box = [bold]Rule.[/bold] If you are unsure whether an action is allowed, do not do it and ask the administration.

lobby-tutorial-lore-title = THE STORY
lobby-tutorial-lore-intro = After the events of the first Half-Life at Black Mesa the Combine, an interdimensional empire, invaded Earth. Earth lost the Seven Hour War in seven hours and capitulated.
lobby-tutorial-lore-breen = Doctor Wallace Breen, the former administrator of Black Mesa, became the puppet administrator of Earth and cooperates with the occupiers. He runs the Citadel, a huge tower in the middle of the city that serves as the Combine headquarters.
lobby-tutorial-lore-freeman = About twenty years later Gordon Freeman wakes from stasis and arrives by train in the city where Half-Life 2 takes place. He becomes the symbol of the Resistance.
lobby-tutorial-lore-world = The game shows what this world is made of: a train station with a checkpoint, a plaza held by Civil Protection, OTA squads, the Nova Prospekt prison and the Outlands beyond the city.
lobby-tutorial-lore-city = On this server the story takes place in City 14. The city is built the same way, but its events are its own, and the character cannot know them in advance.
lobby-tutorial-lore-box = [bold]Context.[/bold] The lore explains the setting. It is not a licence to play knowledge the character does not have.

lobby-tutorial-life-title = LIFE UNDER OCCUPATION
lobby-tutorial-life-intro = Life is hard, frightening and monotonous. People crowd into cramped flats, receive scant rations and work to exhaustion. Any suspicion of disloyalty leads to interrogation, arrest or disappearance.
lobby-tutorial-life-ally = To the Combine people are a resource. Civilians count as labour and as potential traitors, CP keeps order with fear and violence, and OTA feels nothing and works like a merciless machine.
lobby-tutorial-life-blend = Rule one: do not stand out. Keep the curfew, wear the prescribed clothes and do not argue with CP in the street.
lobby-tutorial-life-papers = Rule two: keep your papers. The CID card is your life, and without it you are nobody.
lobby-tutorial-life-work = Rule three: work. The Union provides jobs and punishes absenteeism and sabotage harshly.
lobby-tutorial-life-trust = Rule four: trust nobody. The city is full of informers and provocateurs, the Resistance exists, and it is easy to find and destroy.
lobby-tutorial-life-box = [bold]Survival.[/bold] Attention to detail matters more than courage here: the queue, the papers and a quiet step keep you alive.

lobby-tutorial-roles-title = PICKING A ROLE
lobby-tutorial-roles-intro = After connecting you enter the lobby and pick a role. That choice defines your experience, so do not grab the first one you see.
lobby-tutorial-roles-cp = Civil Protection is the local Combine police. You keep order, check CID cards and punish violators, and in return you get a weapon and limited authority. For cruelty or corruption your own side may remove or execute you.
lobby-tutorial-roles-citizen = A citizen is an ordinary person with no weapon and no authority. The job is to survive, to work and maybe to help the Resistance in secret.
lobby-tutorial-roles-gsr = The Civil Workers Union was created with Combine support to employ the population. Director and worker roles give access to production and logistics. It is a legal life, but with a debt of responsibility to the Combine.
lobby-tutorial-roles-refugee = A refugee in the Outlands is not available at the start. You get there only after death, by lottery, if the character survived and escaped the city. Life there is a constant fight for resources against zombies and Combine patrols.
lobby-tutorial-roles-locked = OTA and Rebels are not available for ordinary selection. The administration hands those roles out for merit or during events.
lobby-tutorial-roles-box = [bold]Tip.[/bold] Do not take a role you are not ready to play: it costs the whole round, not one evening.

lobby-tutorial-antag-title = ANTAGONISTS
lobby-tutorial-antag-intro = Read up on the game and the rules first, and only then take an antagonist. Failing in that role ruins the round for many players, not just for you.
lobby-tutorial-antag-revolutionary = A Resistance revolutionary sabotages, spreads leaflets, stirs up small riots and helps fugitives. He works in the shadows, and a direct clash with CP is suicide for him.
lobby-tutorial-antag-saboteur = A saboteur is an elite Resistance agent, and the target is the Nexus core. You have to get into a guarded area and blow the facility up, which takes a plan, a disguise and help from other players.
lobby-tutorial-antag-rules = An antagonist does not cancel the rules. Fear, death and consequences apply to him exactly as to everyone else.
lobby-tutorial-antag-box = [bold]Warning.[/bold] An antagonist is not a licence for impunity but responsibility for the scene.

lobby-tutorial-rp-title = ROLEPLAY
lobby-tutorial-rp-intro = Roleplay here rests on two simple roles, and almost everything that happens in the city depends on them.
lobby-tutorial-rp-cp = A CP officer is not a kind policeman but a representative of a repressive apparatus. He is cold, bureaucratic and cruel within the limits of decency, and he speaks in stock phrases such as Citizen, show your CID.
lobby-tutorial-rp-cp-tone = He is still not a cartoon villain. Play exhaustion, indifference or fanatical loyalty to the Combine, but do not kill without a reason: the administration will punish that.
lobby-tutorial-rp-citizen = A citizen is a frightened, tired person, and his main emotion is fear. He avoids eye contact with CP, speaks quietly and follows orders.
lobby-tutorial-rp-citizen-life = Play the daily routine: the ration queue, complaints about work, whispers about the Resistance. A citizen's strength is in his story, not in his fists.
lobby-tutorial-rp-box = [bold]Mood.[/bold] Fear and daily life give more scenes than heroism and gunfire.

lobby-tutorial-start-title = QUICK START
lobby-tutorial-start-intro = The first fifteen minutes follow one script, and it is worth knowing it in advance.
lobby-tutorial-start-arrival = You appear at the train station, and a CP officer or a Union employee comes up to you.
lobby-tutorial-start-checkpoint = Go through the checkpoint. You may be asked to introduce yourself, and that is a normal procedure.
lobby-tutorial-start-legend = Say where you came from: City 8, the countryside, another city. Just do not say you are straight out of the game.
lobby-tutorial-start-cid = Show the CID card from your inventory. If there is no card, CP decides the matter, and you may be sent for re-registration.
lobby-tutorial-start-city = Leave for the city and find the ration point. It usually stands on the plaza or in a residential block.
lobby-tutorial-start-job = Apply at the Union office for work. That gives you a legal income and something to do.
lobby-tutorial-start-phases = Watch the announcements. The city has work phases, a curfew and inspections, and breaking the phases leads to trouble with CP.
lobby-tutorial-start-box = [bold]Good luck in City 14.[/bold] Surviving here is already a success.

